derekt75 wrote:
> I had previously assumed that when riding my speed didn't matter and only my steed's did.  This seems false.
When riding, the number of actions you get per turn is equal to the
number of actions your steed gets per turn if you moved on the previous
turn, or the number of actions you get per turn if you didn't move on
the previous turn.

You only get the speed boost from a galloping steed if you were
farmoving (running, travelling, moving with a repeat count) at the end
of the previous turn.

